<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8215"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Scbenson2001<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Scbenson2001<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->6-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 21, 2005 - 8:20 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->The dictionary describes a serial killer as a person who attacks and kills one by one in a series of incidents. BTK fits this definition. Motive is not part of it. If you are saying BTK is not like a normal serial killer you might have a point. However your just stating the obvious, BTK is unlike any case in history.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
