<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8226"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Scbenson2001<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Scbenson2001<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->6-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 21, 2005 - 9:56 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->My point was that it doesn&#39;t matter why or how a killer kills if they commit them over a period of time, one at a time, then by definition THEY ARE A SERIAL KILLER! That is the only requirement! Prototypical of course not he&#39;s been at large for 30 years and communicating with law enforcement. It&#39;s unprecidented. Your theory is just incorrect he is a serial killer.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
