<!--Post: 8285--><!--Time: 1109038687-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8285"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Whatthehell<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Whatthehell<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 21, 2005 - 6:18 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->A AGREE ON THE POSSIBILITY OF SUCH A RATIO IN A SMALLER TOWN BUT THE WICHITA POPULATION IS FAR TOO BIG TO HAVE THAT RATIO NOT BE SIGNIFICANT. THAT IS JUST THE WORK RATIO, CONSIDER THE ODDS OF TWO PEOPLE BEING KILLED AND TWO OTHERS BEING SHOT ALL IN THE SAME FOUR MONTH PERIOD. EVEN WITH TODAYS POPULATION AND OUR NATIONAL AVERAGE OF 4 HOMICIEDS PER EVERY 10,000 PEOPLE ALLOWING FOR 2.57 PEOPLE TO BE KILLED IN WICHITA ON AVERAGE PER MONTH AND BEING 134 PER YEAR. <a href="http://www.nationmaster.com/graph-T/cri_mur_cap" target=_top>http://www.nationmaster.com/graph-T/cri_mur_cap</a> <BR>I DO NOT KNOW HOW MANY THE COLEMAN COMPANY EMPLOYEED IN 1974 BUT TODAY IT IS 1300 AT WICHITA. THAT TRANSLATES TO AN AVERAGE MURDER RATE OF ABOUT .067 MURDERS A YEAR FOR THE COLEMAN EMPLOYEE POPULATION. SO I WOULD THINK THAT STATISTICALLY 2 MURDERS AND TWO SHOOTING IN 4 MONTHS WOULD BE OF A VERY HIGH SIGNIFICANCE. <BR>THE RATIO OF COLEMAN EMPLOYEES 1300 TO THE GENERAL WICHITA POPULATION 336,300 IS ABOUT 1 IN EVERY 259 PEOPLE. <BR> <BR>THANKS FOR MAKING ME DO THE MATH.  <BR>I APPRECIATE THE FEEDBACK.  <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
