<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8291"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:bmodule_244@hotmail.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Bmodule<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bmodule<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 21, 2005 - 6:32 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->&#34;How many do I have to kill, before I get my name in the paper or some national attention? <BR> <BR>Do the cop think that all those deaths are not related? Yes, the M.O. is different in each, but look at the pattern that is developing. The victims are tie up _ most have been women _ phone cut _ bring some bondage mater sadist tendencies _ no struggle, outside the death spot _ no wntness except the Vian&#39;s kids. <BR> <BR>You guess the motive and the victims. <BR> <BR>After a thing like Fox, I come home and go about life like anyone else. And I will be like that until the urge hits me again.&#34; <BR> <BR>Whatthehell <BR> <BR>&#34;you guess the motive&#34;? <BR> <BR>I think you are right. He definately has an alterior motive.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
