<!--Post: 8318--><!--Time: 1109052705-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8318"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 21, 2005 - 10:11 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->The important point is that BTK remains uncaptured; we know who his victims are, we have some names of possible victims. It&#39;s 2005, I call him a serial killer, anyone else can call him what they please, as long as the goal is to capture him. <BR> <BR>When Nancy Fox, Vicki Wegerle and Anna Williams, excuse me, her daughter, can be connected to Coleman, then I&#39;d say you have something to go on. &#40;&#34;Oh Anna, Why Didn&#39;t You Appear?&#34;&#41;. What is the first name of the late Ms. Williams&#39; daughter? If it isn&#39;t &#34;Anna&#34; then I must wonder why this poem title, engendered by BTK, has the name &#34;Anna&#34; in it. <BR> <BR>I don&#39;t for one second buy that BTK was a hit-man or part of a hit-team who was so aroused by his &#34;hit&#34; &#40;I must be behind on my hit-man literature; I thought they usually used firearms, blunt force trauma - which is silent if done properly - or knives, also silent if done properly&#41; that he then &#34;became&#34; a serial killer. The Otero attack had all four victims strangled with their own blind cord. Not a very competent hit man. Additionally, hit men are known for killing quickly then leaving as quickly as possible - and not in the car of whom they&#39;ve just killed! - and not parking said car two blocks away. If the Otero scene was a &#34;hit,&#34; then so was Vicki Wegerle. Think about that. I&#39;m also unaware of any hit man who wrote letters and poems to the police - over a period of years, too. Or is BTK such a genius that he made himself resemble a serial killer &#40;in January, 1974, the term serial killer was not often used&#41; when in fact he was nothing more than a hit man? Of course he wasn&#39;t/isn&#39;t. <BR> <BR>I guess I mean that &#34;does BTK meet the definition of a serial killer or not?&#34; isn&#39;t so important any longer. By the way, a man who murders via strangulation for revenge and repeats the act several times, over a period of years and upon strangers, is, indeed, a serial killer. Now, as to the small matter of putting a name to him...or a residence. Arguing whether he meets &#34;criteria&#34; as a serial killer, at this point in time, isn&#39;t going to catch him. <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8318-->
<!--Post: 8319--><!--Time: 1109052995-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8319"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 21, 2005 - 10:16 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Correction: I do not know if Ms. Anna Williams is &#34;late&#34; or not.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
