<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8321"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 21, 2005 - 10:27 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->From the original post: <BR><i>DO NOT GET ME WRONG BTK IS A SICK MAN. HE HAS A TASTE FOR KILLING AND HAS THE MENTAL AD EMOTIONAL CAPACITY TO KILL AGAIN IF NPT THE PHYSICAL</i>. <BR> <BR>Another term for this is &#34;serial killer.&#34;<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8321-->
<!--Post: 8327--><!--Time: 1109055486-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8327"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:hackenmaster@yahoo.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Wichitan<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Wichitan<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 21, 2005 - 10:58 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Well, I thought it was a great theory.  I can tell you are from wichita, for the simple fact that your down to earth.  I think it could be possible to be the guy next door.  I dont feel he is wandering the streets like jack the ripper.  I think infact he would use his real name, and probably has lived in wichita all his life. But at this point, we can only go one what were are told..which isn&#39;t much.  <BR> <BR>dont forget to post your date!! <BR><a href="http://www.catchbtk.com/discus/messages/11/460.html?1108621037" target=_top>http://www.catchbtk.com/discus/messages/11/460.htm l?1108621037</a> <BR> <BR>wichitan<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8327-->
<!--Post: 8339--><!--Time: 1109067799-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8339"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Ivy_leaguer<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ivy_leaguer<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 22, 2005 - 2:23 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->The BTK Strangler is a serial murderer. The Otero murders comply with the geographic definition of mass murder. However, the psychology of the murderer does not comply with the portrait of a mass murderer. Mass murderers tend to be psychotic, characterized by limited intelligence, lack organization, tend to be careless, impulsive and some commit suicide or expect to die at the crime scene. The Otero murders were committed by a sadistic psychopath who committed four more confirmed murders over a period of twelve years.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8339-->
<!--Post: 8343--><!--Time: 1109079690-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8343"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 22, 2005 - 5:41 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Hi Wichitan - That&#39;s just it. You wrote, <i>I think it could be possible to be the guy next door. I dont feel he is wandering the streets like jack the ripper. I think infact he would use his real name, and probably has lived in wichita all his life.</i> I don&#39;t disagree with this. It&#39;s merely that this is basic Serial Killer 101; guy next door? Bundy, Ridgeway, Gacy, Rifkin &#40;I really hate this guy; he taunted his way through an hour-long television special - had a s-eating grin on his face the whole time&#41;, and so forth. Wandering around like Jack The Ripper? No way! I agree completely. Uses his real name? Yes, I agree. Lived in Wichita all his life? In it or near it &#40;say within ten-fifteen miles&#41;? Yes, I agree. I would add that I believe the possibility exists that BTK now resides a little farther from Wichita than he once did. I don&#39;t mean he&#39;s living in another state, only that it&#39;s more likely now that he&#39;s, say, fifty miles from Wichita, a little more remote. But I can also see him living right there in Wichita proper. <BR> <BR>Since terminology seems to be of interest, I&#39;ll give a few examples, using Ivy Leaguer&#39;s accurate definition. Mass murderers: Charles Whitman&#42;, Kileen, Texas shooter, Klebold and Harris, the guy who shot up the McDonald&#39;s in CA, Dick and Perry, using the pretext, and both knew it was a pretext, of robbery and so forth. <BR> <BR>&#42;There is yet another category, &#34;assassin,&#34; which John Douglas and maybe others are/were trying to promote. Enough with the highly specific categories already. The above named people were mass murderers, most died at the scene. Continuing to create tiny categories makes profiling weaker and weaker and arguments against it stronger. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8343-->
<!--Post: 8348--><!--Time: 1109083678-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8348"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Rocky<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Rocky<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 22, 2005 - 6:47 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Why are all the victims women, with exception to Mr. Otero? You know when I studied psychology in college, it was only after I studied more about the human brain that I could appreciate the possibilites of something going wrong upstairs. I&#39;ve read that a serial killer has a form of obsessive compulsiveness, &#40;the X factor&#41;. Maybe BTK was medicated for a period of time to control his obsessive compulsiveness and then decided to quit taking his medication.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8348-->
<!--Post: 8350--><!--Time: 1109084089-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8350"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Whatthehell<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Whatthehell<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 22, 2005 - 6:54 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->hey all. i think that i made a mistake in nameing the theory &#34;not a real serial killer&#34;. the premise that the first two killings were &#34;grudge&#34; killings and coleman connected, and from this <BR>&#34;a killer is born&#34; seems to be missed due to the poor naming of the theory. sorry. i do believe that he is a serial killer. i just believe that the coleman connection is too strong to cast off. <BR> <BR>thanks for making me think. <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8350-->
<!--Post: 8358--><!--Time: 1109090472-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8358"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Teardrop<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Teardrop<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 22, 2005 - 8:41 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Whatthehell: you may not be all that far off when you say he is not a real serial killer. Initially, his killing of the Otero family may have been grudge based. As his anger was released and the deeds were done, the thrill continued. He realized that he had to kill again to recapture that &#39;high&#39;. It might be akin to someone dreading or disliking to do something, like public speaking or stage performance. After it is over, they felt the personal triumph and the rush of &#39;yes, I was good at that&#39; feeling. Instant addiction. He was an immature killer when he left semen at the scene. As he matured, less and less semen was found. His control over 4 victims, 2 of which were adults, shows profound capabilities on the part of the killer, particularly in his early career. And quite brazen and confident to do all this in the daytime as well. But he does fit the serial killer definition of killing with a cooling off period in between. I believe that 3 homicides are required with a cooling off period. It will be much easier to understand when all facts are known. If ever. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8358-->
<!--Post: 8390--><!--Time: 1109104499-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8390"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Rocky<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Rocky<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 22, 2005 - 12:34 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Hey you know, what the hell, you threw it out there. LOL! I still think this serial killer took a 20 year leave because he was medicated. Were there drugs on the market back then that could have helped this monster the last twenty years? What the hell would you even prescribed to someone like that? Yikes!!! I don&#39;t believe they even had alcohol and drug treatment programs through the employer at that time, did they? Hmmm!<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8390-->
<!--Post: 8634--><!--Time: 1109257642-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8634"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Teardrop<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Teardrop<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 24, 2005 - 7:07 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Mellaril, Haldol, Thorazine, Lithium, Valium, Electroconvulsive shock therapy. A cocktail of any or all would do the trick. One of these drugs prohibits ejaculation so BTK may have been living in a very frustrating time capsule, waiting to escape. Unless someone just happened to run across his records, it would be virtually impossible to locate when and where he may have been hospitalized, if at all. Could he possibly have self medicated by having access to such meds indirectly &#40;in some way associated by employment or otherwise&#41; with a facility or patient? I needed a histamine 2 antagonizer, took my father to the doctor, told him to tell the doctor about his stomach trouble, and voila, he came out with a script for Zantac. Pairing that with a histamine 1 antagonizer, 95% remission was mine in 24 hours. <BR> <BR>BTK could have had a family member with similar behavioral problems, worked in a facility, a drugstore, etc. He is such an experienced cat burglar that he could have easity gotten into a pharmacy and taken what he wanted. There were no cameras in those days. They would have assumed some lowlife junkie was doing the breakins and not an upstanding citizen. Just a thought. He may have been desperate to deal with his issues earlier in his life. <BR> <BR>No one in their right minds would want to take Thorazine or Haldol voluntarily if they knew the actions of the drugs. I feel terrible that I requested Thorazine for some MRs when I worked at a state school. It inhibits serotonin reception, so the person is so unhappy that he cannot act out. It was an effective drug, however, and did not produce a rewarding high like Valium.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8634-->
<!--Post: 8737--><!--Time: 1109302162-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8737"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Rocky<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Rocky<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 24, 2005 - 7:29 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Teardrop: Do you know if it is possible to obtain medical records from a previous employer? Mainly, a previous employer that had a drug and alcohol treatment program. By the way, I appreicate your info, but were these drugs on the market in the 1970&#39;s? <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8737-->
<!--Post: 8739--><!--Time: 1109302773-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8739"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Bakerwood<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bakerwood<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 24, 2005 - 7:39 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Rocky, <BR>Google the term &#34;HIPPA&#34;. <BR> <BR>Nobody with an aversion to courtrooms would even think of opening an employee&#39;s records to any other one without a court order.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8739-->
<!--Post: 8749--><!--Time: 1109305851-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8749"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Rocky<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Rocky<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 24, 2005 - 8:30 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Bakerwood I work with HIPPA forms on a daily basis, but only if the Plaintiff has signed it &#40;now days&#41;! My question being, back in the 70&#39;s or even 80&#39;s what were the standard procedures or policies for employment related drug therapy programs? If I recall correctly, those records were a lot more obtainable. Maybe, the WPD should go Coleman or Boeing avenue! Regardless, of HIPPA now in the 21st century I would think a Subpoena would safice it to say!<!--/Text--></td></tr>
